 #edb/ref 17592186133877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051085 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051085 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051085 #edb/ref 1031 "The Curl of a Vector Field" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051085 #edb/ref 1033 2132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051085 #edb/ref 1034 1.1334058414679022 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051085 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7fdf89be-7454-5a23-9d34-17c62e869eea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186177137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177135 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0eade32f-b760-5926-93db-b12fa72570ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177137 #edb/ref 1080 "-k" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177137 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177137 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "abc12917-c767-5961-875f-8b79c0ea4558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179548 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8745" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179548 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\nabla\\times(3\\mathbf{F} + \\mathbf{G})$ at the point $(-1,1,0)$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = 3x\\,\\mathbf{i} + y^2z\\,\\mathbf{j} + 2\\,\\mathbf{k}, \\quad (\\nabla\\times\\mathbf{G})(x,y,z) = 3y^2\\,\\mathbf{i} + 4z\\,\\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179548 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3a28f359-71aa-5b9b-b55c-802374e6821f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179548 #edb/ref 1074 "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\times (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\times \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\times \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =∇\\times (3F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 3x & {y}^{2}z & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3x)]k \\\\  & =(0-{y}^{2})i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (3F+G) & =3∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =3[-{y}^{2}\\,i]+[3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k] \\\\  & =-3{y}^{2}\\,i+3{y}^{2}\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =(3{y}^{2}-3{y}^{2})\\,i+4z\\,j+k \\\\  & =4z\\,j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,1,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-1,1,0) & =4(0)\\,j+k=k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179550 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8931" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179550 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) =  \\langle 0, y-z, x-y\\rangle$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z) = x+y.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times \\mathbf F = \\langle 0,\\,-1,\\,0\\rangle, \n\\quad\n\\nabla f = \\langle 1,\\, 1,\\, 0\\rangle,\n$$\n\ncalculate $\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F)$ at the point $(-1,1,3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179550 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e27e6735-4d50-5c26-a20d-44454ddcdef3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179550 #edb/ref 1074 "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times(f\\,\\mathbf F) = f \\nabla \\times \\mathbf {F}+   \\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla f \\times \\mathbf F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & y-z & x-y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (y-z)]\\,i-[1\\cdot (x-y)-0\\cdot (0)]\\,j+[1\\cdot (y-z)-1\\cdot (0)]\\,k \\\\  & =(x-y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j+(y-z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x+y)⟨0,-1,0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-(x+y),0⟩+⟨x-y,\\,y-x,\\,y-z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x-y,\\,-2x,\\,y-z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(-1,1,3) & =⟨(-1)-1,\\,-2(-1),\\,1-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186367394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186489265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179689 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Curl of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties" #edb/