n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,1,3) & =⟨-\\frac{1(3)}{(1)^{2}},-\\frac{3}{1},0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263010 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨2,-1,2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263010 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263010 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0100d61e-bd3a-57c3-ac46-ef0541e36274" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263295 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-1,2,1⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263295 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263295 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2042f10b-c030-5440-b613-21a9c012d3c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264961 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-1,1,0⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264961 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264961 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1e6b082-e166-5ac8-86bc-ab551fbc182d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265169 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,1,2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265169 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265169 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f7d5658b-f678-5414-8532-e4f1e07ce37d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265179 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-2,-2,0⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265179 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265179 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f923aa32-197d-5f20-bcd7-cb503c0d99f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186265169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186265179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186264961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265621 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d8585553-bc3d-59dd-bec0-062d6e8ffbec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266091 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266091 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131473" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266091 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266091 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,y,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=xyz.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨yz,xz,xy⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,1,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266091 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ded29f1-5616-5a96-a16e-84431dafd500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266091 #edb/ref 1074 "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ yz & xz & xy \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡z & y & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[(xz)(0)-(y)(xy)]i-[(yz)(0)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)(xy)]j+[(yz)(y)-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)(xz)]k \\\\  & =-x{y}^{2}\\,i+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,j+(z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =xyz⟨0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩+⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-xyz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z,0⟩+⟨-x{y}^{2},xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},-xyz\\operatorname{sin}⁡z+xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡z,z{y}^{2}-xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-x{y}^{2},-xy(z\\operatorname{sin}⁡z-\\operatorname{cos}⁡z),z({y}^{2}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,1,0) & =⟨-1,-(0\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0),0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366836 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366836 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105711" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366836 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366836 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $∇\\times (F-G)$ at the point $(0,2,1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\,i+xy\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=-i+2z\\,j-x\\,k.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366836 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f694a45-bb80-5fc5-bc87-30958ae2f792" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366836 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡z & 0 & xy\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(0)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡z)]k \\\\  & =(x-0)i-(y-\\frac{1}{z})j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =x\\,i+(\\frac{1}{z}-y)j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =x\\,i+(\\frac{1}{z}-y)j-[-i+2z\\,j-x\\,k] \\\\  & =x\\,i+(\\frac{1}{z}-y)j+i-2z\\,j+x\\,k \\\\  & =(x+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{z}-y-2z)j+x\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,2,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(0,2,1) & =(0+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{1}-2-2(1))j+0\\,k \\\\  & =i-3\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366837 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366837 #edb/ref 107