c62b5eb0bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388216 #edb/ref 1074 "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F+G) & =∇\\times (2F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =2∇\\times F+∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ xyz & xy & {z}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz)]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-xy)j+(y-xz)k \\\\  & =xy\\,j+(y-xz)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (2F+G) & =2∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =2[xy\\,j+(y-xz)\\,k]+xy\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =2xy\\,j+2(y-xz)\\,k+xy\\,j-x\\,k \\\\  & =3xy\\,j+(2y-2xz-x)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-1,2,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (2F+G))(-1,2,0)=-6\\,j+5\\,k.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186388222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388217 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "785f634a-3bb0-5c9e-b015-ebbcf506a3c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388218 #edb/ref 1080 "-6\\,i+5\\,j" #edb/ref 1759218604541